    "Ballot positions captured exactly as printed (A1, A2, A3, A4, B1, C1, C2, C3, C4, D1-D4, E1-E4). NJ county-line ballots use column letters per office (A=Senate, B=House, C=County Commissioners, D=Female County Committee, E=Male County Committee) and row numbers within each column. Note that A1/B1/C1 appear in BOTH the DEM and REP race objects (same column letter used on each party's separate ballot).",
    "Slate labels captured as printed under each candidate via the 'party' field per advisor guidance (e.g., 'Camden County Democrat Committee, Inc.', 'South Jersey Progressive Democrats', 'America First Always', 'Camden County Regular Republican Party', 'America First Republicans', 'By The People, For The People'). The schema's 'party_context' carries the macro Dem/Rep distinction.",
    "Write-in slots: NJ ballots show a write-in line under EVERY candidate column. To avoid combinatorial explosion, ONE write-in placeholder per race is recorded rather than per-column slot. Strict scoring may differ — flag as authoring choice.",
    "Members of the Board of County Commissioners 'Vote for Two (2)' captured as vote_for_n=2.",
